# UI Components Refactor & Consistency Rules

Before creating or modifying UI in TSX/JSX under `app/`:

1. Read and follow the DRY refactor guidance in [refactor-ui-bot.md](mdc:.cursor/commands/refactor-ui-bot.md).
2. Align with the design system in [Docs/UI_UX_doc.md](mdc:Docs/UI_UX_doc.md).
3. Reuse existing primitives first; only create new components if no good fit exists.

## Required Practices
- Prefer composition over inheritance; keep components small and prop-driven.
- Normalize surface across primitives:
  - `variant`: primary, secondary, ghost, destructive
  - `size`: sm, md, lg
  - Shared states: `disabled`, `loading`
- Enforce a11y: semantic roles/landmarks, labels, focus rings (focus-visible), keyboard nav.
- Use lucide-react icons only.

## Reusable Primitives (use/extend instead of ad-hoc HTML)
- Button (existing): action triggers with `variant`/`size` normalization
- Card (existing): content container; prefer `elevation` and `padding` props

## High-Frequency Atoms to Introduce/Use
- SectionHeader: `title`, `subtitle?`, `icon?`, `actions?`; sizes sm/md/ld
- DataRow: `label`, `value`, `icon?`, `muted?`; dense/comfortable
- EmptyState: `title`, `description`, `action?`, `icon?`; compact/standard
- FormField: wraps label → control → hint/error with proper ARIA wiring

If a page uses repeated raw Tailwind blocks matching these patterns, replace them with the components above instead of duplicating markup.

## Migration Aids (optional but recommended)
- Use the search heuristics in [refactor-ui-bot.md](mdc:.cursor/commands/refactor-ui-bot.md) to find duplicate patterns (headers, cards, empty states, label+input stacks).
- Map occurrences to target components and refactor in-place.

## Acceptance
- No new raw repeated HTML+Tailwind for headers/cards/forms/empty states.
- Variants and sizes are consistent across primitives.
- Focus styles, spacing, and tokens match [Docs/UI_UX_doc.md](mdc:Docs/UI_UX_doc.md).

